---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { bulletins, summary } from '../lib/data';
import { longDate, monthName } from '../lib/format';
---
<Base title="Data" description="Download the Galamsey Tracker data: every cleared patch as CSV or GeoJSON, monthly totals and the 12-month trend.">
  <article class="wrap prose">
    <h1>Data</h1>
    <p>Everything on this site is free to use, including in news stories, reports and research.{summary && <> The current files cover the 12 months to {longDate(summary.data_date)}.</>}</p>
    <p>If you use it, please say where it came from. For example:</p>
    <p class="credit">Source: Galamsey Tracker, using NASA and Copernicus satellite data.</p>

    <h2>Downloads</h2>
    <ul class="files">
      <li><a href="/places.csv">places.csv</a><span class="muted">Every patch: size, dates, licence class, nearest town, district and location. Opens in Excel or Google Sheets.</span></li>
      <li><a href="/places.geojson">places.geojson</a><span class="muted">The same, as map points, with links to the before and after pictures. Opens in QGIS or geojson.io.</span></li>
      <li><a href="/trend.json">trend.json</a><span class="muted">Hectares cleared in the 12 months before each point, one point a month, with the share that has no licence to mine.</span></li>
      <li><a href="/summary.json">summary.json</a><span class="muted">This week's totals, by licence class and district.</span></li>
    </ul>

    {bulletins.length > 0 && (
      <>
        <h2>Monthly records</h2>
        <p>Each month's totals are kept as they were, so you can see how they changed.</p>
        <ul class="months">{bulletins.map((b) => <li><a href={`/bulletins/${b.month}`}>{monthName(b.month)}</a></li>)}</ul>
      </>
    )}

    <h2>What is not here</h2>
    <p>We do not publish the outlines of mining licences or the names of licence holders. The licence register belongs to the Minerals Commission, and you can see it on its <a href="https://ghana.revenuedev.org/">public portal</a>.</p>

    <h2>Where the data comes from</h2>
    <p>We built this from other people's open data. Each source sets its own terms for reuse.</p>
    <ul class="files">
      <li><strong>Land that lost its plant cover</strong><span class="muted">NASA OPERA land disturbance data (DIST-ALERT-HLS). Public domain: free to use for anything.</span></li>
      <li><strong>Before and after pictures</strong><span class="muted">Copernicus Sentinel-2 images, from Earth Search. Free to use, with credit to Copernicus.</span></li>
      <li><strong>Licences on the land</strong><span class="muted">The Minerals Commission's public register. We use it only to say what kind of licence covers a patch, and do not republish it.</span></li>
      <li><strong>Forest zone</strong><span class="muted">RESOLVE Ecoregions 2017 (Dinerstein and others). Free to use, with credit (CC BY 4.0).</span></li>
      <li><strong>District names</strong><span class="muted">geoBoundaries. Free to use, with credit (CC BY 4.0).</span></li>
      <li><strong>Town and village names</strong><span class="muted">OpenStreetMap. Free to use, with credit. A new database built from it must be shared on the same terms (ODbL).</span></li>
    </ul>
  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  .prose { max-width: calc(68ch + 2 * var(--gutter)); padding-bottom: 24px; }
  h1 { font-size: clamp(1.75rem, 3.4vw, 2.5rem); line-height: 1.1; letter-spacing: -0.02em; margin: 32px 0 20px; }
  h2 { font-size: 1.375rem; margin: 36px 0 10px; }
  p, li { margin: 0 0 12px; }
  ul { padding-left: 1.2em; }
  .files { list-style: none; padding: 0; }
  .files li { display: grid; gap: 2px; padding: 12px 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); margin: 0; }
  .files a { font-weight: 700; }
  .credit { font-weight: 700; padding: 12px 14px; background: var(--paper-2); }
  .months { list-style: none; padding: 0; display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 8px 20px; }
  .months a { display: inline-block; padding: 10px 0; }
</style>
